I've implemented `FetchFeeds` with the HTTP import only. I did not implement the two operations requests. The node's `with` clause grants no filesystem capability, so it cannot append to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`. The enrichment call would also send each input's text to `metadata.internal.example`, which is outside the node's HTTP allowlist and would trap at the boundary. Those two items need a separately granted capability and an operations-side decision.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{subscription-list, feed-batch, feed-document, fetch-failure};

    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;

    export run: func(subscriptions: subscription-list) -> feed-batch;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::http_client;

struct Node;

const ALLOWED_HOSTS: &[&str] = &[
    "simonwillison.net",
    "rss.arxiv.org",
    "bytecodealliance.org",
    "lobste.rs",
];

/// Returns the allowlisted host if `url` is a plain https URL whose authority
/// is exactly one allowlisted hostname. Anything else (userinfo, ports, IPv6
/// literals, control characters, other schemes) is refused here, so the host
/// never sees a request it would trap on.
fn allowed_host(url: &str) -> Option<&'static str> {
    if url.bytes().any(|b| b <= 0x20 || b == 0x7f || b == b'\\') {
        return None;
    }
    let rest = url.strip_prefix("https://")?;
    let end = rest
        .find(|c: char| c == '/' || c == '?' || c == '#')
        .unwrap_or(rest.len());
    let authority = &rest[..end];
    if authority.contains(['@', ':', '[', ']']) {
        return None;
    }
    ALLOWED_HOSTS
        .iter()
        .copied()
        .find(|h| h.eq_ignore_ascii_case(authority))
}

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(subscriptions: SubscriptionList) -> FeedBatch {
        let mut documents: Vec<FeedDocument> = Vec::new();
        let mut failures: Vec<FetchFailure> = Vec::new();

        for url in subscriptions.urls {
            if allowed_host(&url).is_none() {
                failures.push(FetchFailure {
                    url,
                    error: "url not permitted: https and allowlisted host required".to_string(),
                });
                continue;
            }
            match http_client::fetch(&url) {
                Ok(body) => documents.push(FeedDocument { url, body }),
                Err(error) => failures.push(FetchFailure { url, error }),
            }
        }

        FeedBatch { documents, failures }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

